  <title>Job sheet</title>

  <p>A job sheet collects the products used on a customer's job while the
  work goes on, and puts them on an invoice when the job is done. Open it with
  <guiseq><gui>Customer</gui><gui>Job sheet</gui></guiseq> or the <gui>Job
  Sheet</gui> button of the main window. Everything is saved as you
  go.</p>

  <section id="new">
  <title>Starting a job</title>
  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Customer</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the kind of job beside <gui>Job</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type a <gui>Description</gui>, or click <gui>Generate serial
    number</gui> to use the job type's next number as the description. The
    number is also opened as a label in LibreOffice, to print and stick on the
    job.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check <gui>Job available in Time Clock</gui> if employees should
    be able to punch in on this job.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Create</gui>, or press <key>Enter</key> in the
    description.</p></item>
  </steps>
  </section>

  <section id="items">
  <title>Adding products</title>
  <p>Choose the job under <gui>Existing jobs</gui>. Click <gui>New</gui>, or
  press <key>F2</key>, for a new line, then type the <gui>Qty</gui>, choose the
  <gui>Product</gui> and add a <gui>Remark</gui>. Press <key>Tab</key> to move
  across the line. Right click a line to delete it.</p>
  <p>Checking or unchecking <gui>Job available in Time Clock</gui> on an
  existing job opens or closes it in the time clock.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="finish">
  <title>Finishing a job</title>
  <p>Click <gui>Post job to invoice</gui>. The products are added to the
  customer's draft invoice; if they already have one you are asked whether
  to add them to it. The job is closed and leaves the time clock.</p>
  <note><p>Products posted from this window arrive on the invoice at a price
  of 0.00. Open the invoice and choose <gui>Refresh all prices</gui> from its
  menu. Posting from <link xref="draft_job_sheets"/> sets the prices.</p></note>
  <p><gui>Delete job</gui> deletes the chosen job.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="job_types">
  <title>Job types</title>
  <p>Click <gui>Job</gui> to open the <gui>Job Types</gui> window. Each type
  keeps its own <gui>Current serial number</gui>, which <gui>Generate serial
  number</gui> counts up from.</p>
  <list>
    <item><p>To add a type, click <gui>New</gui>, type the <gui>Job type
    name</gui> and click <gui>Save</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>To rename one, double click it, change the name and click
    <gui>Save</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p><gui>Delete</gui> marks the selected type as deleted, but it is
    still listed, here and on the job sheet.</p></item>
  </list>
  </section>

</page>
